<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="MoonlightInVermont-Eb-Theme" spTempo="70">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1944 (written earlier; sometimes dated 1943)
Composer:	Karl Suessdorf
Lyricist:	John M. Blackburn
Form:	24-bar AABA, with an optional
	two-bar ending
Style:	Jazz ballad
Key:	Db major (reported original key;
	commonly played in other keys)

The song was published in 1944 and introduced in a 1944
recording by Margaret Whiting with the Billy Butterfield
Orchestra. Blackburn’s unrhymed lyrics use compact,
haiku-like images of Vermont’s seasons;
some sources date the writing to 1943, while publication
and first recording are dated 1944.</spComments>
